#!/bin/bash
#PBS -N cgm_push
#PBS -P 11704243
#PBS -j oe
#   qsub -l select=1:ncpus=8:mem=32gb -l walltime=00:30:00 \
#        -o logs/98_push_report.log scripts/pbs/98_push_report.pbs            # -> qdev
source "${REPO:-$HOME/workspace/Project_CGM/CGM-OutlierMIA-master}/scripts/pbs/env.sh"
set +e
module load git/2.39.2
cd "$REPO"
{
  git add -A
  echo "staged: $(git diff --cached --numstat | wc -l) files"
  git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'
Rebuild the report as an experiment record, and check its numbers against the artefacts

The page was a results summary. It is now the decision chain: each section states the
question, the design, the observation, what it rules out and why the next experiment
followed, and carries its own status.

Corrections the rebuild forced, all from the artefacts rather than the write-ups:

- The 80-subject swarm was under Question 1. It is a Question 2 artefact — it needs
  both models — and its own summary.json calls itself exploratory. Moved, relabelled.
- 0.664 was the headline. It is the excluding-1142 sensitivity analysis; the primary
  result is 0.680 and the page now says which is which everywhere both appear.
- "79 of 80 within 0.50-0.52" understates the lower tail. The array runs 0.4807-0.5182.
- The relative gap is not reproducible as 0.27% vs 0.11%. Recomputed per replicate
  against each arm's own median distance it is 0.250% and 0.122%; the discrepancy is
  stated on the page rather than resolved silently.
- Three-channel results now carry PARTIAL, 44 of 123, and the note that replicate 1's
  arms are 13 against 18 and no longer day-matched.
- Seven-day h256 is BLOCKED, not training: 11 checkpoints, then sampling died with CUDA
  OOM at h256 x T=2016, and nothing is in the queue.
- The two-channel outlier vote is COMPLETE: all four seeds landed at 14:01 today,
  22 subjects survive all four, 84.6% against 66.7% for the single-channel run.
- The width sweep no longer implies anything about seven days. It rules out capacity
  for the one-day three-channel configuration and says so.

New interactions all answer a question rather than decorate one: the broken-vs-correct
attack construction (both measured, the broken one reaching +0.14 that is entirely
release identity), the copy_paste ceiling simulator, the min-vs-mean reduction, the
rank-vs-magnitude switch, the quality gate in front of the seven-day leakage numbers,
and the nearest-neighbour dilution geometry.

Every number lives in one DATA object. validateDataConsistency() checks the page against
itself on load; scripts/check_report_data.py re-derives 110 of them from the artefacts
and reports the 2 that have no artefact rather than skipping them.

Not done: no browser or node on this machine, so the page was never rendered and the
palette validator was never run. Verification was static — a JS tokenizer pass, a
selector/id reference check, and the two data checks above.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
MSG
  git log --oneline -1
  git -c credential.helper="store --file=$HOME/.git-credentials-github" \
      push origin main 2>&1 | sed -E 's#//[^@]*@#//***@#g'
  echo "push exit ${PIPESTATUS[0]}"
} 2>&1 | tee logs/98_push_report.live.log
